From fc5f38cb9e59b288e07119b069d6a9ce4c46da1e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 25 Jul 2026 13:06:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix: bound Lara call concurrency instead of fully serial,
 raise maxDuration
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Live test showed a new failure mode after making everything sequential
(previous commit): translating a proposal with a featured experience
plus 3 suggested add-ons completed the first experience in full
(content+sections+facts) but left the rest partially or entirely
untranslated — the exact signature of the serverless function hitting
its execution timeout partway through, not a Lara error.

- New mapWithConcurrency() helper: runs a bounded number of calls at
  once instead of Promise.all (everything, which triggered Lara rate
  limiting) or a sequential loop (safe but too slow once several
  experiences each have several facts/sections).
- syncFullExperienceTranslations: sections and facts within one
  experience now run 3 at a time.
- /api/translate-proposal-experiences: experiences now run 2 at a time,
  and maxDuration is raised to 60s so there's enough runway even when a
  proposal pulls in several experiences worth of content.

